{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"octo","tool":"query","arguments":{"folder":"/home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33","query":"Two states are bisimilar if every transition can be matched to a bisimilar state in both directions; one step bisimilarity introduction","topK":6},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"scope=both folder=/home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33\n\n1. **Cslib.LTS.Bisimilarity** (definition, cslib, distance=0.760)\n   Bisimilarity of states in labelled transition systems\n   Given two labelled transition systems $\\mathrm{lts}_1$ and $\\mathrm{lts}_2$ on state types $\\mathrm{State}_1$ and $\\mathrm{State}_2$ with a common label type $\\mathrm{Label}$, two states $s_1 \\in \\mathrm{State}_1$ and $s_2 \\in \\mathrm{State}_2$ are bisimilar if there exists a bisimulation relation $r : \\mathrm{State}_1 \\to \\mathrm{State}_2 \\to \\mathrm{Prop}$ such that $r$ relates $s_1$ and $s_2$.\n   `Cslib.LTS.Bisimilarity.{u_1, u_2, u_3} {State₁ : Type u_1} {State₂ : Type u_2} {Label : Type u_3}   (lts₁ : Cslib.LTS State₁ Label) (lts₂ : Cslib.LTS State₂ Label) : State₁ → State₂ → Prop`\n   at: Cslib.Foundations.Semantics.LTS.Bisimulation:113\n   file: /home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33/.lake/packages/cslib/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean\n\n2. **Cslib.LTS.IsHomBisimulation** (definition, cslib, distance=0.761)\n   Homogeneous bisimulation relation for a labelled transition system\n   Given a labelled transition system $\\mathrm{lts}$ on a state type $\\mathrm{State}$ and a label type $\\mathrm{Label}$, a relation $r : \\mathrm{State} \\to \\mathrm{State} \\to \\mathrm{Prop}$ is a homogeneous bisimulation if it is a bisimulation between $\\mathrm{lts}$ and itself. That is, whenever $r$ relates two states $s_1$ and $s_2$, then for every label $\\mu$, the following two conditions hold:  1. For every transition $s_1 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_1'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}$, there exists a transition $s_2 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_2'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}$ such that $r$ relates $s_1'$ and $s_2'$. 2. For every transition $s_2 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_2'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}$, there exists a transition $s_1 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_1'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}$ such that $r$ relates $s_1'$ and $s_2'$.\n   `Cslib.LTS.IsHomBisimulation.{u_3, u_4} {Label : Type u_3} {State : Type u_4} (lts : Cslib.LTS State Label)   (r : State → State → Prop) : Prop`\n   at: Cslib.Foundations.Semantics.LTS.Bisimulation:110\n   file: /home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33/.lake/packages/cslib/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean\n\n3. **Cslib.LTS.IsBisimulation** (definition, cslib, distance=0.763)\n   Bisimulation relation for labelled transition systems\n   Given two labelled transition systems $\\mathrm{lts}_1$ and $\\mathrm{lts}_2$ on state types $\\mathrm{State}_1$ and $\\mathrm{State}_2$ with a common label type $\\mathrm{Label}$, a relation $r : \\mathrm{State}_1 \\to \\mathrm{State}_2 \\to \\mathrm{Prop}$ is a bisimulation if, whenever $r$ relates two states $s_1$ and $s_2$, then for every label $\\mu$, the following two conditions hold:  1. For every transition $s_1 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_1'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}_1$, there exists a transition $s_2 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_2'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}_2$ such that $r$ relates $s_1'$ and $s_2'$. 2. For every transition $s_2 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_2'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}_2$, there exists a transition $s_1 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_1'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}_1$ such that $r$ relates $s_1'$ and $s_2'$.  In other words, the transitions from related states mimic each other, and the reached derivatives are again related.\n   `Cslib.LTS.IsBisimulation.{u_1, u_2, u_3} {State₁ : Type u_1} {State₂ : Type u_2} {Label : Type u_3}   (lts₁ : Cslib.LTS State₁ Label) (lts₂ : Cslib.LTS State₂ Label) (r : State₁ → State₂ → Prop) : Prop`\n   at: Cslib.Foundations.Semantics.LTS.Bisimulation:75\n   file: /home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33/.lake/packages/cslib/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean\n\n4. **Cslib.LTS.HomBisimilarity** (definition, cslib, distance=0.770)\n   Homogeneous bisimilarity\n   Given a labelled transition system $\\mathrm{lts}$ on a state type $\\mathrm{State}$ and a label type $\\mathrm{Label}$, two states $s_1, s_2 \\in \\mathrm{State}$ are homogeneously bisimilar if they are bisimilar in the sense of the bisimilarity relation on the same LTS $\\mathrm{lts}$ with itself.\n   `Cslib.LTS.HomBisimilarity.{u_3, u_4} {Label : Type u_3} {State : Type u_4} (lts : Cslib.LTS State Label) :   State → State → Prop`\n   at: Cslib.Foundations.Semantics.LTS.Bisimulation:126\n   file: /home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33/.lake/packages/cslib/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean\n\n5. **Cslib.LTS.Bisimilarity.follow_fst** (theorem, cslib, distance=0.786)\n   Bisimilarity preserves transitions: following a transition from the first state\n   Given two labelled transition systems $\\mathrm{lts}_1$ and $mathrm{lts}_2$ on state types $\\mathrm{State}_1$ and $\\mathrm{State}_2$ with a common label type $\\mathrm{Label}$, if states $s_1$ and $s_2$ are bisimilar, and there is a transition $s_1 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_1'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}_1$, then there exists a state $s_2'$ such that $s_2 \\xrightarrow{\\mu} s_2'$ in $\\mathrm{lts}_2$ and $s_1'$ and $s_2'$ are bisimilar.\n   `Cslib.LTS.Bisimilarity.follow_fst.{u_1, u_2, u_3} {State₁ : Type u_1} {State₂ : Type u_2} {Label : Type u_3}   {lts₁ : Cslib.LTS State₁ Label} {lts₂ : Cslib.LTS State₂ Label} {s₁ : State₁} {s₂ : State₂} {μ : Label} {s₁' : State₁}   (hr : lts₁.Bisimilarity lts₂ s₁ s₂) (htr : lts₁.Tr s₁ μ s₁') :   ∃ s₂', lts₂.Tr s₂ μ s₂' ∧ lts₁.Bisimilarity lts₂ s₁' s₂'`\n   at: Cslib.Foundations.Semantics.LTS.Bisimulation:132\n   file: /home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33/.lake/packages/cslib/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean\n\n6. **Cslib.LTS.«term_~[_,_]_»** (definition, cslib, distance=0.789)\n   Bisimilarity notation\n   The notation $s \\sim[\\mathit{lts}_1, \\mathit{lts}_2] s'$ denotes that the states $s$ and $s'$ are bisimilar with respect to the two explicitly given labeled transition systems $\\mathit{lts}_1$ and $\\mathit{lts}_2$.\n   `Cslib.LTS.«term_~[_,_]_» : Lean.TrailingParserDescr`\n   at: Cslib.Foundations.Semantics.LTS.Bisimulation:118\n   file: /home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33/.lake/packages/cslib/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean\n\nLower distance is closer."}],"structured_content":{"hits":[{"source":"cslib","distance":0.7595815658569336,"name":"Cslib.LTS.Bisimilarity","kind":"definition","moduleName":"Cslib.Foundations.Semantics.LTS.Bisimulation","signature":"Cslib.LTS.Bisimilarity.{u_1, u_2, u_3} {State₁ : Type u_1} {State₂ : Type u_2} {Label : Type u_3}\n  (lts₁ : Cslib.LTS State₁ Label) (lts₂ : Cslib.LTS State₂ Label) : State₁ → State₂ → Prop","docstring":"Two states are bisimilar if they are related by some bisimulation. ","informalName":"Bisimilarity of states in labelled transition systems","informalDescription":"Given two labelled transition systems $\\mathrm{lts}_1$ and $\\mathrm{lts}_2$ on state types $\\mathrm{State}_1$ and $\\mathrm{State}_2$ with a common label type $\\mathrm{Label}$, two states $s_1 \\in \\mathrm{State}_1$ and $s_2 \\in \\mathrm{State}_2$ are bisimilar if there exists a bisimulation relation $r : \\mathrm{State}_1 \\to \\mathrm{State}_2 \\to \\mathrm{Prop}$ such that $r$ relates $s_1$ and $s_2$.","sourceStart":113,"sourceStop":116,"localPath":"/home/auras/Projects/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.33/.lake/packages/cslib/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean","githubUrl":"https://github.com/leanprover/cslib/blob/v4.32.0/Cslib/Foundations/Semantics/LTS/Bisimulation.lean#L113-L116"},{"source":"cslib","distance":0.7614665627479553,"name":"C